In January, the Sundance Film Festival will present its first edition in a new home of Boulder, Colorado, and two months ahead of the anticipated launch, the team has revealed the first VIP guest being welcomed into the fold: Dior .

Parfums Christian Dior has officially partnered with Sundance Institute for the purpose of supporting female filmmakers and storytellers. In doing so, they've created the Miss Dior x Women at Sundance Institute Award as a way to recognize &#8220;a breakthrough cultural force whose bold vision is reshaping the filmmaking landscape.&#8221; The honor will be doled out to a talent on the rise as selected by a yet-to-be-announced curated committee and presented by longtime Dior ambassador Natalie Portman during January's main event. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories General News Steven Spielberg and Kate Capshaw's Hearthland Foundation Donates $3M to Sundance Institute (Exclusive) Movies Sundance Institute Taps Tracy Brady for Chief Marketing, Brand and Communications Role

Also under the pact, they've created the Women at Sundance Institute Miss Dior Momentum Fellowship. The fellowship, created for &#8220;mid-career storytellers who demonstrate artistic excellence and a strong commitment to independent film, will support six artists on their second or third feature film projects through year-round support with direct non-recoupable grants, mentorship, coaching, cohort gatherings, bespoke creative support, networking and a curated Sundance experience. They'll also get the true Sundance experience beyond Boulder through access to Sundance Institute educational and peer communities via the Artist Accelerator Program, ELEVATE professional development sessions, Sundance Collab opportunities and the Sundance Institute alumni network.

But wait, there's more: the Sundance and Dior initiative launches will be the toast of a new event set to take place during the 2027 film festival &#x2014;&#xA0;the Women's Celebration Brunch presented by Dior. That's where Portman will present the prize in front of a gathering of film industry insiders, press, creators and other VIP guests. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#8220;The stories we tell have the power to shape how we see ourselves and one another. This is why supporting women storytellers is so important, not only because their voices deserve to be heard, but because they bring perspectives that enrich our understanding of the world. When a belief in emotion, independence, and conviction meets a commitment to authentic storytelling, we create more than opportunities for artists; we help ensure that women continue to shape culture through the stories they choose to tell,&#8221; said Portman, who serves as the face of the Miss Dior fragrance. &#8220;For me, Miss Dior has always represented the courage to embrace your own voice with optimism, independence, and conviction. I'm proud to see this spirit come to life through the partnership with Sundance Institute, celebrating women whose creativity will continue to inspire future generations.&#8221;

Added Michelle Satter , founding senior director of artist programs for the Sundance Institute: &#8220;At Sundance Institute, we believe every woman deserves the freedom to tell her story in her own voice, on her own terms. This shared commitment comes to life through the inaugural Miss Dior x Women at Sundance Institute Award, honoring a filmmaker whose creative vision makes a meaningful impact, and our ongoing Momentum Fellowship, which supports women directing their second or third fiction or nonfiction feature. Together, we're investing in the voices, visions and stories that will move our culture forward. We look forward to celebrating this partnership at the Women's Celebration Brunch presented by Dior during our upcoming Sundance Film Festival in Boulder.&#8221;

The new film about the founder of the Hershey Company begins with a loving, beautifully lit close-up of one of the company's signature products, a Hershey's Kiss. That tells you pretty much everything you need to know about this effort produced in part by Hershey Entities and distributed by Angel Studios . Starring Finn Wittrock ( American Horror Story ) in the title role, Hershey is a blandly sanitized biopic that's as sickly sweet as the candies the company sells. Being released for Thanksgiving, it essentially serves as a feature-length product placement. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The film, which an opening title card informs us is "based on the unlikely true story," begins in 1870 with a young Milton (James Kelly) growing up in a Mennonite community in rural Pennsylvania. After the tragic death of his younger sister and the abandonment of the family by his dreamer father ( Alan Ruck ), he begins working for a kindly confectioner, Joseph Royer ( Richard Kind , at his most twinkly), who teaches him candy-making methods. Related Stories TV AMC's 'Mayfair Witches: Salem Coven' Gets December Debut as Catherine Zeta-Jones, Carrie-Anne Moss Tease 'Kill Jackie' and 'Yaga' at NYCC TV Angel Studios' 'Homestead: The Series' Sets Season 2 Premiere Date and Cast (Exclusive) Hershey The Bottom Line Will give you cavities. Release date : Wednesday, November 25 Cast : Finn Wittrock, Alexandra Daddario, Alan Ruck, Richard Kind, David Costabile, James Kelly, Michael Moreland Milligan, Daniel David Stewart, Joel Brady, Francesca Faridany, Dina Spybey-Waters, John Hans Tester, Heléne Yorke, Mark Ashworth, Isabel Van Natta Director : Mark Waters Screenwriters : Sharon Paul, Timothy Michael Hayes Rated PG, 1 hour 50 minutes

Milton is soon inventing original candies and eventually opens his own shop specializing in (oh, the irony) caramels. The shop fails but the young entrepreneur is undeterred, and he tries again with a store in Lancaster, Pennsylvania, that takes off after a bulk order from a visiting Englishman.

The episodic screenplay by Sharon Paul and Timothy Michael Hayes chronicles Hershey's rise to prominence in dutiful fashion, including his eventual transition to producing chocolates. This comes about after a visit from a salesman representing a German chocolate company, who, after being rejected by Hershey because the product tastes bitter, warns him, "I think you're missing out on what's next." Sure enough, Hershey changes his mind, realizing that all the chocolate needs is some milk to make it taste better. The rest, as they say, is history. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

"Caramels are a fad, but chocolate is permanent," Hershey confidently tells his associates.

On his way to becoming a chocolate titan, Hershey meets the adorable Kitty ( Alexandra Daddario ), with their love story fueling much of the film's second half. He turns the village where he grew up into the company town that still bears his name, treating his employees benevolently (the violent labor disputes that occurred in later years are ignored) and, at the urging of his wife, opening a school for impoverished youth that still exists today. (Left unmentioned is the fact that admission was restricted to whites; Black students weren't admitted until 1968.)

Another major plot element is Kitty's serious illness, which prevents her from having children and results in numerous scenes that find her nearly collapsing while Milton looks on concernedly.

Flavorlessly directed by Mark Waters (far past his Freaky Friday and Mean Girls glory days), Hershey never succeeds in coming to life, playing like the sort of candy-coated dramatized film that would find its most receptive audiences at the Hershey Story Museum in Pennsylvania. Every scene plays out exactly as you'd expect, with conflicts resolved serendipitously and Hershey benefiting from fortunate strokes of luck, including a malfunctioning machine producing what became the Hershey's Kiss and the couple miraculously avoiding a planned voyage on the Titanic (they dance to their good fortune, which, considering what happened to the poor souls onboard, seems a bit tacky). blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Wittrock, eventually outfitted with a period-perfect moustache, does a reasonably good job but is ultimately unable to overcome the script's deficiencies. Daddario fares better, conveying a tender warmth and playfulness that infuse the film with much of its heart. (Strangely, Wittrock eventually receives old age makeup treatment while Daddario looks virtually the same throughout). The supporting players, including David Costabile ( Billions ) as a composite business competitor, do exactly what's expected of them.

The film ends in predictable fashion, with vintage photographs of the real-life figures and present-day footage of the school and its grateful students. That's followed by one of those annoying "Pay It Forward" pitches, gamely delivered by Wittrock and Daddario, urging us to pour more money into the studio's coffers under the guise of philanthropy.

BAFTA has blessed its breakthrough class of 2026.

The organization has revealed the roster of talent &#x2014; actors and directors to writers and below-the-line standouts &#x2014; selected to shine as its BAFTA Breakthrough U.S. cohort for the year. It's a list of 14 &#8220;rising creatives&#8221; paving their way through film, television and games and &#8220;helping shape the future of the screen industries.&#8221;

The list (in alphabetical order by first names with mention of their breakout project) includes Union County filmmaker Adam Meeks, The Burbs creator Celeste Hughey, Heated Rivalry heartthrob Connor Storrie , Nuisance Bear documentary director Gabriela Osio Vanden, 1923 and Frisco King costume designer Gaby Acosta, Night Nurse filmmaker Georgia Bernstein, Obsession star Inde Navarrette , Clair Obscur: Expedition 33 game lead writer and voice and localization producer Jennifer Svedberg-Yen, Despelote game lead developer Juli&#xE1;n Cordero, Backrooms filmmaker Kane Parsons , Bandi composer Marcus Norris, Barbara Forever documentary editor Matt Hixon, Bedford Park filmmaker Stephanie Ahn and South Midnight game writer Zaire Lanier. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories TV LGBTQ Representation on TV Dropped in 2025-26, GLAAD Study Finds Movies 'Wet,' Starring Connor Storrie, Rebecca Ferguson and Odessa A'zion, Acquired by Lionsgate

BAFTA Breakthrough, supported by Apple TV, is now in its seventh year. It's described as the arts charity's flagship talent initiative, and is designed to support creatives at a pivotal point in their careers. The cohort receives access to professional development, industry connections and opportunities to build their networks within the creative community. They take part in a year-long program, which features one-on-one meetings and career guidance, full BAFTA voting membership, access to BAFTA events and screenings and networking opportunities here and abroad. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#8220;This year's cohort reflects the imagination, ambition and distinct perspectives that continue to push our industries forward. At a time when emerging creatives face increasing challenges in finding opportunity, mentorship and a path forward, BAFTA is proud to create a space where talent can be recognized, supported and connected to a broader creative community,&#8221; explained BAFTA North America executive director Courtney LaBarge Bell. &#8220;Each member of this cohort brings a unique point of view and a commitment to their craft that we believe deserves to be seen and championed. Over the next year, we look forward to supporting their growth, creating meaningful connections and helping open doors as they continue to build lasting careers.&#8221;

The roster was selected by a jury that included Adolpho Veloso, Alysa Nahmias, Arseni Khachaturan, Julia Kim, Peter Teschner, Rolfe Kent, Sonia Kennebeck, Bella Gonzales and Nana Mensah for film and TV, and Bethany Higa, Bhamini Lakshminarayan, Del Walker, Mai Koythong, Michael Surya, Nick Apostolides, Robert Dominguez and Virginia Leo for games. Alums include Stephanie Economou, HIKARI, Nava Mau, Bao Nguyen, Fernando Reyes Medina, Karrie Shirou Shao, Erica Tremblay, Cheyenne Pualani Morrin, Sean Wang, Erika Ishii, Eva Victor and Chase Infiniti.

&#8220;The idea rose up in me unstoppably,&#8221; says Russell T Davies of his new series Tip Toe . The creator, who was first put on the television map with his groundbreaking 1999 series Queer as Folk , had been working on another project when he found himself so increasingly alarmed by the state of the world and the cacophony of conservative and bigoted voices on the internet that he rushed home to Manchester to start writing a new script.

&#8220;I'm well known as a gay writer and activist, and when you are that person in this modern world you automatically get called a pervert online,&#8221; he explained during a recent THR Presents panel. &#8220;I get called a pedophile and a groomer daily, you can just search for my name and there it is. I'm always thinking about terrible things that might happen to me every single day.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories TV 'The Traitors' Star Ben McDonnell on 'New Blood' Set Secrets and Alan Cumming: "You Can Never Break Character" Movies 'THR Presents' Q&A With Hana Jusic, Director of Croatian Oscar Contender 'God Will Not Help'

That real-life horror became the story of Tip Toe , which follows opens with the violent hanging death of a queer bar owner at the hands of his conservative next-door neighbor and then jumps back in time to trace the seeds of the tragedy. The bar owner is played by Alan Cumming , who Davies refers to as a &#8220;sleeping giant.&#8221; Though Cumming has become known more recently for his bubbly hosting gigs on the Traitors franchise, Davies felt strongly that the actor had more to show audiences. The two first met over 20 years ago on a business lunch and have been trying to work together ever since.

&#8220;I said yes as soon as he told me about the story,&#8221; says Cumming. &#8220;I feel like it's a fateful thing that [our working together] happened in this way, with a show that means so much to both of us. In a very primal way it's about who we are as queer men in our 60s.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Davies created the show with the UK's Channel Four, and while he was ferociously writing the scripts he says he &#8220;warned&#8221; the network that they were coming. &#8220;When I eventually handed the script in to them, they commissioned the show within seven days. Nothing happens that fast. But seven days later in the middle of their Christmas dinner they said yes &#x2014; that's how much they felt it was important.&#8221;

Watch the rest of the conversation between Cumming and Davies in the video above. This edition of THR Presents is sponsored by Starz .

Denis Villeneuve sat down for an interview with GQ magazine in the days before Robert Pattinson was officially announced as the new James Bond and broke down the most important qualities he was looking for in the search for his 007. The &#8220;Dune&#8221; and &#8220;Blade Runner 2049&#8221; director is helming Bond 26 at Amazon MGM Studios.

&#8220;At the end of the day, the truth is, no matter who I choose, some people will be excited and others will be disappointed,&#8221; Villeneuve said about the search for his Bond actor, which reportedly included the likes of Callum Turner, Josh O'Connor, Nicholas Hoult and Jack Lowden before the director's &#8220;Dune: Part Three&#8221; star Pattinson won the part. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Brandi Carlile's All-Requests Tour Isn't Just a Magnificent Stunt, but an Unusually Moving Transaction Between Performer and Audience: Concert Review

So what gave Pattinson the edge over his fellow Bond audition-mates? &#8220;The first quality is that I need to believe that this man is a killer, because more than a spy, Bond is an assassin,&#8221; Villeneuve said about what his Bond actor needed. &#8220;I need that kind of anger deep in the eye. It's not everybody who has that.&#8221;

&#8220;I need someone who has that kind of unapologetic panache, someone that when he comes into the room, everything starts to gravitate around him, that kind of strong charisma and someone that has a lot of sensuality as well and that people are attracted to&#x2026; someone who has dark humor, someone that has pleasure in being in deep shit, someone who is not afraid to put his hand in the mud,&#8221; the director continued. &#8220;I need someone that is strong, muscular, someone that is a force. And someone, of course, who has a deep intelligence in the eyes, someone that is always ahead of us.&#8221;

Pattinson clearly checked off all the above boxes to become Villeneuve's Bond. The director issued a statement upon the news of Pattinson's official casting in which he expressed &#8220;deep gratitude the remarkable actors who joined us on this journey.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#8220;We were surrounded by extraordinary talent, but there can only be one 007,&#8221; Villeneuve added. &#8220;I am overjoyed to welcome Robert Pattinson as our new James Bond. He has the timeless soul of 007 and brings a spirit that is completely new. I cannot wait to begin."

Pattinson shared in his own statement: "James Bond is one of the most legendary characters in cinema, and to be entrusted with 007 is the honor of a lifetime&#8230; To say this role is a dream come true is an understatement. I couldn't be more excited about this partnership and the work ahead with this fantastic team."

Villeneuve and Pattinson will begin filming Bond 26 sometime in 2027.

EXCLUSIVE: After Endgame: A Comedy About Chess , the Fringe solo show from comedian Kevin James Doyle , will become his fourth comedy special, out February 11 on his YouTube channel.

After Endgame is a lesson in both life and chess from someone who has taught over 6,500 chess lessons. Doyle takes the audience on a journey across the globe as he is flown to the vibrant city of Singapore at the behest of a mysterious investor. There, he finds himself imparting chess wisdom to some of the world's wealthiest individuals. Tensions rise as he navigates these high-stakes players, both on and off the chessboard. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Touring Comedian Nate Jackson Unveils Dates For 2027 Miracle Baby Tour Podcast Gianmarco Soresi Talks Debut Netflix Special, Global Comedy Explosion, Role Of "Sh*t Talk" In Keeping Comics Honest - Comedy Means Business Podcast

Doyle became a chess instructor in New York City 15 years ago, around the same time he started doing stand-up comedy . Following his experience in Singapore, he knew he had to tell the story on stage &#x2014; a tale of real-life game of deception, with feints and intrigue, which he analyzes with lessons he learned from studying chess. In constructing the show, he drew inspiration from films like House of Games and The Color of Money , as well as the Off-Broadway sleight-of-hand magic show Ricky Jay and His 52 Assistants . Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

Doyle performed After Endgame to critical acclaim at the Edinburgh Fringe in 2024, followed by 2025 dates in Chicago, Columbus, Denver and Los Angeles, as well as four weeks off-Broadway at the Soho Playhouse in New York City. Now the show will find a wider audience as Doyle's fourth comedy special streaming on his YouTube channel starting Feb 11, 2027. After Endgame is directed by his longtime friend and collaborator, Cory Cavin .

Doyle is Creative Producer at SoHo Playhouse, where he founded and leads SoHo Playhouse Jr., the theater's children's theater and education program. He previously co-wrote and starred in the long running Off-Broadway production How to Be a New Yorker and has also performed at the Edinburgh Festival Fringe with The 30 Year Old Virgin and Diary of a Bald Kid &#x2014; which were taped as specials &#x2014; and Wild Card . blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Doyle is otherwise known for co-hosting The Bradshaw Boys , a Sex and the City podcast featuring appearances by all four principal actresses, and co-creating Great Times with Cory and Kevin , a New York City comedy show running since 2014.

However, Adeyemi has shared a range of experiences in regards to the making of the film, at one point saying that she will not watch the movie and at another saying that the process of the adaptation was one of the worst things she has ever had to live through . In light of those previous comments, it seemed unlikely that there would be any positive commentary from Adeyemi ahead of the movie's debut, but now, she has taken fans by surprise with a brand-new post sharing considerably more positive thoughts on the project. Check out her exact comments below.

Adeyemi took to Instagram this week with her surprisingly positive and uplifting message about the upcoming theatrical release of Children of Blood and Bone , writing, among other things, &#8220;This entire franchise started as an impossible dream. It was impossible from the start, and as we near the world premiere for this project, it still feels impossible that a girl could run into ceramic tiles of the Orisha in a tiny gift shop in Brazil and then create a world that a new generation of kids could get lost in&#8230;This film was made for all of us. It's the culmination of hard work from so many people — from the director @gpbmadeit to the hundreds of people in front of and behind the camera who worked themselves to the bone to honor and amaze you. It is meant to celebrate you and uplift you, and moving forward, that is all I want to do.&#8221; The post ends, &#8220;I can't wait see you at the theaters.&#8221;

Understandably, fans have been caught by surprise with this message, and the comments in response to Adeyemi's post make that clear. One commenter wrote, &#8220;No disrespect girl, but didn't you say you're not gonna support? I hope they paid you triple,&#8221; and another said, &#8220;This is just getting confusing. You probably shouldn't have released anything in the first place. Because this is not a good look.&#8221; However, many commenters are just happy to see Adeyemi now showing support for the movie, with one person writing, &#8220;I'm glad to see you promoting this Tomi, truly. I'm very excited to see this movie, especially since I read the first book back in 2018. My only sadness is that we might not be able to see the second and third books adapted. I hope that does change because this series is truly amazing and deserves to be seen on the big screen.&#8221;

Will you be going to see Children of Blood and Bone , and have the conversations around the adaptation swayed your opinion at all? Share your thoughts down below.

