EXCLUSIVE : Filmmaker Stacey Muhammad , who directed the most episodes on series Cross and The Greatest , as well as six on Amazon comedy Harlem , is attached to direct feature biopic Wells , chronicling the life of pioneering investigative journalist, civil rights leader, suffragist, and NAACP co-founder Ida B. Wells.

The project, which is the first narrative feature about the icon, brings together producers Share, IndieScene, Autumn Bailey Entertainment, and Wild Mercy Pictures.

The film, which is in development, will chart Wells' journey from post-Reconstruction Memphis, &#8220;where the murder of three of her friends transforms her journalism into a mission, through her groundbreaking anti-lynching investigations, exile, international advocacy in Britain, and later fight for women's suffrage.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories News Fubo Shares Jump As Disney-Controlled Pay-TV Operator Posts Record Fiscal 2026 Revenue Executives Jennifer Dodge and Traci Balthazor To Oversee Animation Across Both Paramount And Warner Bros. As Bill Damaschke Departs Studio

